        "response": "Based on the provided context, here are the specific hepatic-related assessments and criteria in the TJ301 trial:\n\n---\n\n## Hepatic Laboratory Assessments\n\nThe following liver-related parameters are included in the **Routine Clinical Chemistry** panel (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 85):\n\n- **Alanine transaminase (ALT)**\n- **Aspartate transaminase (AST)**\n- **Alkaline phosphatase (AP)**\n- **Gamma glutamyl transferase (GGT)**\n- **Bilirubin \u2013 total**\n- **Bilirubin \u2013 direct** *(only if total bilirubin is outside the normal range)*\n- **Albumin**\n- **Protein \u2013 total**\n\n---\n\n## Hepatic Exclusion Criteria\n\nSubjects are excluded if they meet any of the following hepatic thresholds (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 35 & p. 11):\n\n- **Without primary sclerosing cholangitis (PSC):** Serum transaminases >2.5\u00d7 ULN, alkaline phosphatase >2.5\u00d7 ULN, or clinically significant abnormalities in synthetic liver function tests\n- **With PSC diagnosis:** Serum transaminases >3\u00d7 ULN, alkaline phosphatase >3\u00d7 ULN, or total bilirubin >1.5\u00d7 ULN judged clinically significant by the investigator\n- Known concurrent **acute or chronic viral hepatitis B or C** infection (Exclusion Criterion 16)\n\n---\n\n## Infectious Disease Screening (Hepatic Viruses)\n\nThe following hepatic virus screenings are also required (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 87):\n\n- **HBV** \u2013 Hepatitis B Surface Antigen\n- **HCV** \u2013 Hepatitis C Antibody",
