        "response": "The study has two primary endpoints:\n\n**1. Efficacy Endpoint:**\nClinical and endoscopic remission at **Week 12**, defined as:\n- Full Mayo score \u2264 2\n- No individual subscore > 1\n- Rectal bleeding subscore = 0\n\nThis is a binary outcome (remission status = yes/no) analyzed by a **logistic regression model** with treatment and randomization-stratification factors (prior corticosteroids treatment and consent to participate in PK substudy) as fixed effects, and baseline full Mayo score as a covariate. Patients with missing remission status data are assumed to be **not in remission**. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 68; p. 7; p. 30)\n\nThe full Mayo score ranges from 0\u201312 (higher = worse) and incorporates both clinical signs/symptoms and endoscopic scoring of colonic mucosal inflammation. (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 30)\n\n**2. Safety Endpoint:**\n- Adverse events\n- Vital signs\n- 12-lead Electrocardiography (ECG)\n- Clinical safety laboratory abnormalities\n\n(Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p. 7)",
